l dikes and contacts be","platform":"ground","year":2011,"line_km":16.0},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":110,"text":"various properties of Decar drill core (Table 9-4), including resistivity, natural radioactivity, and magnetic susceptibility.","platform":"borehole","year":2011},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":110,"text":"Prefeasibility Study Effective Date: September 6, 2023 9.4 Downhole Surveys Downhole geophysical surveys were used to characterize various properties of Decar drill core (Table 9-4), including resistivity, natural radioactivity, a","platform":"borehole","year":2023},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":111,"text":"9.4.2 Induced Polarization (IP) and Resistivity Downhole induced polarization and resistivity (DCIP) surveying was completed in September and October 2011 and c","platform":"borehole","year":2010},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":112,"text":"Vertical resistivity and chargeability profiling was achieved by placing a standard current and potential electrode down a single borehole, with measurements taken","platform":"borehole","year":2012},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":113,"text":"Source: Caracle Creek, 2011. 9.4.3 Magnetics Magnetic susceptibility data was routinely collected as part of all diamond dr","year":2011},{"method":"magnetics","page":114,"text":"Positional data is measured by an on-board magnetometer and inclinometer sensors, which allow the OTV data to be corrected to true azimuth and dip."}],"targets":[{"page":90,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"serpentinized peridotite and dunite, showing that at least three chromite showings are associated with very high magnetic response (Pezzot and Vincent, 1982); however, no further chromite- focused exploration was completed."},{"page":106,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"They also suggested that the Baptiste, Sid, and Van targets all occur within, or close to the borders of, magnetic highs. A correlation between strong magnetics and awaruite mineralization is consistent with the strongly magnetic nature of awaruite and, more d"},{"page":109,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Results from this survey confirmed and refined the contacts of two magnetic lows interpreted to be associated with a lithologic contact in the southwest and a zone of incipient serpentinization in the northeast, both considered unfavourable for awaruite minera"},{"page":112,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Results indicate awaruite-bearing peridotite has generally low resistivity (<120 \u2126\u00b7m) and high chargeability (>25 mV/V) (Palich and Qian, 2012). More resistive zones, with or without chargeability, are broadly associated with unmineralized altered dykes and gr"},{"page":121,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"A few holes showed noticeably lower average susceptibility (\u22645 SI units) that correlate with higher proportions of non-magnetic lithology like Fe-carbonate altered peridotite, listwani"}]},"rock":{"rqd":{"n":4,"min":14.0,"max":60.0,"median":54.0,"page":118,"text":"Study Effective Date: September 6, 2023 Recovery averaged 90.9% and rock quality designation (RQD) ranges from 43-63%, for an average of 50.6%, corresponding to rock quality designation on the boundary separating poor from"},"overburden_m":{"n":1,"min":12.0,"max":12.0,"median":12.0,"page":202,"text":"Davis Tube magnetically recoverable (DTR) nickel is the nickel content recovered by magnetic separation using a Davis Tube, followed b"},"density_samples":{"n":1,"min":978.0,"max":978.0,"median":978.0,"page":210,"text":"Study Effective Date: September 6, 2023 14.5 Density Assignment A total of 978 specific gravity measurements were used to assign bulk density values to the lithologic domains."},"slope_angle_deg":{"n":2,"min":20.0,"max":20.0,"median":20.0,"page":254,"text":"This results in an overall slope angle of approximately 20\u00b0, which can be further optimized in the next stage of study."},"density_low":{"n":1,"min":3.0,"max":3.0,"median":3.0